    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="translation-of-the-memorandum">

                <pb facs="0009" n="[III]" xml:id="pgIII"/>

                <head>Translation of the memorandum of the party claimant</head>
                <p rendition="#center">TO THE</p>
                <p rendition="#center">HONORABLE ARBITRATOR, MR. T. M. C. ASSER,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Counselor to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the
                        Kingdom<lb/>of the Netherlands, etc.</hi>,</p>
                <p rendition="#center">IN THE</p>
                <p rendition="#center">ARBITRATION AGREED UPON BY THE EXCHANGE OF NOTES BETWEEN
                    THE<lb/>REPRESENTATIVES OF THE TWO HIGH CONTRACTING POWERS, DULY<lb/>AUTHORIZED
                    TO THAT EFFECT, DATED SEPTEMBER 3, 1900, TO<lb/>ADJUST THE DIFFERENCES BETWEEN
                    THE GOVERNMENT OF<lb/>THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA, PARTY CLAIMANT,<lb/>AND THE
                    IMPERIAL GOVERNMENT OF RUSSIA,<lb/>PARTY DEFENDANT, RELATIVE TO THE<lb/>ARREST
                    AND SEIZURE OF THE<lb/>AMERICAN VESSELS</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">“CAPE HORN PIGEON,” “JAMES HAMILTON
                        LEWIS,” “C. H. WHITE,”<lb/>AND “KATE AND ANNA.”</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center">HERBERT H. D. PEIRCE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counsel for
                        the United States.</hi></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
